{
  // Static-asset Worker for the built Jekyll site (`_site_build`), added by
  // Cloudflare's autoconfig bot in #3 and deployed by Cloudflare Workers
  // Builds.
  //
  // The service name MUST NOT be `algosize`. That is the API Worker's
  // service (see worker/wrangler.toml), which GitHub Actions deploys from
  // `.github/workflows/worker.yml`. With both configs named `algosize`, the
  // two pipelines deploy different Workers to the same service and the last
  // one to run wins — so an ordinary site change could silently replace the
  // live API, and an API deploy could replace the site.
  //
  // Related: wrangler resolves its config by walking UP the directory tree,
  // so this file also shadows worker/wrangler.toml for any wrangler command
  // run from inside `worker/`. Every wrangler invocation in the repo
  // therefore passes `--config wrangler.toml` explicitly. See DEPLOY.md §2.0.
  //
  // THIS CONFIG CANNOT DEPLOY FROM CI AS THINGS STAND, and the failing
  // "Workers Builds: algosize" check on every branch is exactly that. The
  // build log:
  //
  //   Executing user deploy command: npx wrangler versions upload
  //   ✘ [ERROR] The directory specified by the "assets.directory" field in
  //     your configuration file does not exist:
  //       /opt/buildhome/repo/_site_build
  //
  // `_site_build` is a LOCAL artifact — the only thing that creates it is
  // start.sh (`bundle exec jekyll build --destination ../_site_build`), which
  // is the Replit dev startup script. It is not committed and nothing in CI
  // produces it. The Cloudflare build trigger ("Deploy non-production
  // branches": root directory `/`, branch includes `*` except main) has an
  // EMPTY build command and goes straight to `npx wrangler versions upload`,
  // so wrangler looks for a directory that was never built.
  //
  // Nothing in this repo can make that build pass — the build command lives in
  // the Cloudflare dashboard, not here. Run by hand from a tree where start.sh
  // has already produced _site_build, `npx wrangler versions upload` succeeds
  // and uploads a VERSION of algosize-site (it does not route traffic; that
  // needs `wrangler versions deploy`), which is the same command failing in CI
  // purely for want of the directory.
  //
  // Worth checking before "fixing" this in the repo: the live marketing site
  // is built by .github/workflows/jekyll.yml and served by GitHub Pages
  // (DEPLOY.md §1), with only /api/* routed to the real Worker — so this
  // config is very likely deploying a second copy of a site nobody reads.
  // Confirm with `wrangler deployments list --name algosize-site` plus a check
  // for zone routes bound to it; if it holds no routes, this file earns
  // nothing but a red check on every PR and the shadowing hazard above.
  //
  // Two ways out, both dashboard-side: delete the trigger (nothing is lost —
  // Pages already deploys the site and .github/workflows/worker.yml already
  // deploys the API), or give it a real build command
  // (`cd site && bundle install && bundle exec jekyll build -d ../_site_build`)
  // if per-branch site previews are actually wanted.
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "algosize-site",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-11",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "assets": {
    "directory": "_site_build"
  },
  "compatibility_flags": [
    "nodejs_compat"
  ]
}
